{
  "rules": [
    "When sentiment history shows a recent spike (0.67 or 1.0) followed by a drop to zero, the model systematically underestimates volatility and fails to capture subsequent mean-reversion crashes; apply a downward correction of 5-8% to the forecasted path.",
    "The model exhibits a strong upward bias during periods of high sentiment (0.67+), predicting steady growth where true outcomes show sharp reversals; reduce the slope of the forecast curve by 40-50% when recent sentiment peaks are followed by zero readings.",
    "In volatile regimes characterized by alternating high and zero sentiment, the model's linear extrapolation leads to significant overshoots at the horizon; apply a convexity correction that penalizes long-term forecasts more heavily as volatility increases.",
    "When the last 3 days of history show a downward trend coinciding with declining sentiment (0.20->0.00), the model fails to anticipate further drops and should be adjusted downward by approximately 15-20% relative to its baseline projection."
  ]
}
